                                        "entry_id": "e7cec706-a61c-3dd1-987b-75148816845a",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "In a sheepish way; shyly; meekly; bashfully; self-consciously; with embarrassment."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "cf616788-9441-489e-9fe7-df7c1606736e",
                                                "sense_id": "1d2c0654-bd50-3de6-948d-b94762f57b4f",
                                                "text": "But Frank Fairbanks, a retired public administrator, had to sheepishly acknowledge that he had grass. “Unfortunately, like many of our central Phoenix neighbors, we have a green lawn which consumes more water than xeriscape,” he told the paper."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "6f26939a-11f3-4921-b3e5-54dae9c178df",
                                                "sense_id": "1d2c0654-bd50-3de6-948d-b94762f57b4f",
                                                "text": "Renton’s big mistake is sheepishly to offer Sick Boy his stolen share 20 years on: £4,000 in a crumpled brown envelope. “What am I supposed to buy with that?” rages Sick Boy bitterly later. “A time machine?”"
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    }
                                ]
